    "body": "When starting the node with pruning enabled (e.g. `-prune=550`) on a node with full chain history or pruning many files at once, `FindFilesToPrune` and `FindFilesToPruneManual` previously called `PruneOneBlockFile` once per file.\n\nBecause `PruneOneBlockFile` iterated over the entire m_block_index for each file, this was an O(M * N) operation (M = files to prune, N = total blocks). When pruning a full chain (~5,770 files and ~972k blocks), this triggered ~5.6 billion iterations and froze the node running on a Pi 5 for ~10 minutes on startup while holding `cs_main`.\n\nThis PR replaces `PruneOneBlockFile` with `PruneBlockFiles(const std::set<int>&)`, which collects all candidate files and prunes them in a single O(M + N) pass over `m_block_index` using a compact dynamic `bitfield (std::vector<bool>)`. Also skips entries without block or undo data to avoid unneeded checks and prevent file 0 pruning from dirtying header-only or already-pruned index entries. The new signature is analogous to `UnlinkPrunedFiles({file_number});`.\n\nBenchmarked with ~972k blocks and 5,770 files to prune:\n- x86_64 (i7-8665U @ 1.90 GHz): 75.1s -> 14.7ms (~5,100x speedup)\n- ARM64 (Raspberry Pi 5): 606.0s -> 26.3ms (>3,500x speedup)\n\nAdd unit test `blockmanager_prune_block_files_batch` to verify batch pruning, empty set no-ops, and clean dirty-set behavior. Update caller tests in `blockmanager_tests` and `rescan_tests`.",
